## 3. Reading Input Values Using JavaScript

One of the most important things in form handling is reading the value entered by the user.

JavaScript uses the `.value` property to read or update the value of many form controls.

### Example 1: Reading a text input

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body>

    <input type="text" id="username" placeholder="Enter your name">

    <button type="button" id="showButton">Show Name</button>

    <p id="result"></p>

    <script>
        const usernameInput = document.getElementById("username");
        const showButton = document.getElementById("showButton");
        const result = document.getElementById("result");

        showButton.addEventListener("click", function () {

            const username = usernameInput.value;

            result.textContent = "Welcome " + username;
        });
    </script>

</body>
</html>
```

**Expected behavior:**

If the user enters `Prajwal` and clicks the button:

```text
Welcome Prajwal
```

### Understanding the important line

```javascript
const username = usernameInput.value;
```

- `usernameInput` refers to the input element.
- `.value` retrieves the current value entered by the user.
- The retrieved value is stored in `username`.

**Remember:** The `.value` of a normal text input is a string, even if the user enters digits.

Example:

```javascript
const age = document.getElementById("age").value;

console.log(typeof age);
```

If the input contains `21`, the output is:

```text
string
```

If you need a number, convert it:

```javascript
const age = Number(document.getElementById("age").value);
```

For numeric input, `valueAsNumber` is another option:

```javascript
const age = document.getElementById("age").valueAsNumber;
```

An empty or invalid numeric input can produce `NaN` with `valueAsNumber`.

### Example 2: Updating an input value

```html
<input type="text" id="username">

<button type="button" id="fillButton">Fill Name</button>

<script>
    const username = document.getElementById("username");
    const button = document.getElementById("fillButton");

    button.addEventListener("click", function () {
        username.value = "Prajwal";
    });
</script>
```

When the button is clicked, the input displays `Prajwal`.

**Difference:**

```javascript
input.value;              // Read the value
input.value = "Hello";    // Change the value
```

