## 9. Complete Form Validation Project

Let's create a registration form with the following rules:

1. Name is required.
2. Name must contain at least 3 characters.
3. Email is required and must have a valid email format.
4. Password must contain at least 8 characters.
5. Confirm password must match the password.
6. Terms and conditions must be accepted.
7. Display clear error or success messages.

### Complete runnable code

Save this as `form-validation.html` and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>Registration Form</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #f2f2f2;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 400px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 25px;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }

        input:not([type="checkbox"]) {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px;
            margin: 8px 0 15px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        button {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 12px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        .error {
            color: red;
        }

        .success {
            color: green;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <div class="container">

        <h2>Registration Form</h2>

        <form id="registrationForm" novalidate>

            <label for="name">Full Name</label>
            <input type="text" id="name" name="name"
                   autocomplete="name"
                   aria-describedby="nameError">
            <small id="nameError" class="error"></small>

            <br><br>

            <label for="email">Email</label>
            <input type="email" id="email" name="email"
                   autocomplete="email"
                   aria-describedby="emailError">
            <small id="emailError" class="error"></small>

            <br><br>

            <label for="password">Password</label>
            <input type="password" id="password" name="password"
                   autocomplete="new-password"
                   aria-describedby="passwordError">
            <small id="passwordError" class="error"></small>

            <br><br>

            <label for="confirmPassword">Confirm Password</label>
            <input type="password" id="confirmPassword"
                   name="confirmPassword"
                   autocomplete="new-password"
                   aria-describedby="confirmError">
            <small id="confirmError" class="error"></small>

            <br><br>

            <label>
                <input type="checkbox" id="terms" name="terms">
                I accept the terms and conditions
            </label>

            <br><br>

            <button type="submit">Register</button>

            <p id="result" aria-live="polite"></p>

        </form>

    </div>

    <script>

        // 1. Select the form and its input elements

        const form = document.getElementById("registrationForm");

        const nameInput = document.getElementById("name");
        const emailInput = document.getElementById("email");
        const passwordInput = document.getElementById("password");
        const confirmPasswordInput =
            document.getElementById("confirmPassword");

        const terms = document.getElementById("terms");

        const result = document.getElementById("result");


        // 2. Select error message elements

        const nameError = document.getElementById("nameError");
        const emailError = document.getElementById("emailError");
        const passwordError = document.getElementById("passwordError");
        const confirmError = document.getElementById("confirmError");


        // 3. Handle form submission

        form.addEventListener("submit", function (event) {

            // Prevent normal browser form submission
            event.preventDefault();

            // Clear previous messages
            nameError.textContent = "";
            emailError.textContent = "";
            passwordError.textContent = "";
            confirmError.textContent = "";
            result.textContent = "";

            // Read and clean the values
            const name = nameInput.value.trim();
            const email = emailInput.value.trim();
            const password = passwordInput.value;
            const confirmPassword = confirmPasswordInput.value;

            // Track whether the form is valid
            let isValid = true;


            // 4. Validate name

            if (name === "") {
                nameError.textContent = "Name is required.";
                isValid = false;
            }
            else if (name.length < 3) {
                nameError.textContent =
                    "Name must contain at least 3 characters.";

                isValid = false;
            }


            // 5. Validate email

            if (email === "") {
                emailError.textContent = "Email is required.";
                isValid = false;
            }
            else if (!emailInput.validity.valid) {
                emailError.textContent = "Enter a valid email address.";
                isValid = false;
            }


            // 6. Validate password

            if (password.length < 8) {
                passwordError.textContent =
                    "Password must contain at least 8 characters.";

                isValid = false;
            }


            // 7. Confirm password

            if (confirmPassword === "") {
                confirmError.textContent =
                    "Please confirm your password.";

                isValid = false;
            }
            else if (password !== confirmPassword) {
                confirmError.textContent =
                    "Passwords do not match.";

                isValid = false;
            }


            // 8. Validate terms checkbox

            if (!terms.checked) {
                result.textContent =
                    "Please accept the terms and conditions.";

                isValid = false;
            }


            // 9. Display final result

            if (isValid) {

                result.textContent =
                    "Registration form is valid!";

                result.className = "success";

                console.log("Name:", name);
                console.log("Email:", email);

            }
            else {

                result.textContent =
                    "Please correct the errors above.";

                result.className = "error";

            }

        });

    </script>

</body>
</html>
```

### Expected behavior

**Case 1: Empty form**

```text
Name is required.
Email is required.
Password must contain at least 8 characters.
Please confirm your password.
Please accept the terms and conditions.
```

**Case 2: Passwords do not match**

```text
Passwords do not match.
```

**Case 3: All fields are valid**

```text
Registration form is valid!
```

### Understanding the execution flow

When the user clicks Register:

1. The browser attempts to submit the form.
2. Because the form has `novalidate`, its automatic constraint validation is bypassed for this submission.
3. The JavaScript `submit` listener executes.
4. `event.preventDefault()` prevents the normal submission.
5. Previous error messages are cleared.
6. Input values are read.
7. Each validation condition is checked.
8. If any condition fails, `isValid` becomes `false`.
9. The final condition displays either an error or success message.

### Dry run

Suppose the user enters:

```text
Name: Prajwal
Email: prajwal@example.com
Password: javascript123
Confirm Password: javascript123
Terms: Checked
```

| Step | Condition | Result |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Is name empty? | No |
| 2 | Is name shorter than 3 characters? | No |
| 3 | Is email valid? | Yes |
| 4 | Is password at least 8 characters? | Yes |
| 5 | Do passwords match? | Yes |
| 6 | Are terms accepted? | Yes |
| 7 | Is `isValid` still true? | Yes |

Final output:

```text
Registration form is valid!
```

**Important project note:** This is client-side validation for learning and user feedback. It does not create an account or send information to a server. A real application must validate again on the server and handle passwords securely. Never log or store raw passwords unnecessarily.

