## 11. Constraint Validation API

HTML form controls expose properties and methods that let JavaScript inspect built-in validation rules.

### 11.1 `checkValidity()`

Returns `true` if the control or form satisfies its validation constraints; otherwise, it returns `false`.

```javascript
const form = document.getElementById("myForm");

console.log(form.checkValidity());
```

### 11.2 `reportValidity()`

Checks validity and asks the browser to display its validation feedback when constraints are not satisfied.

```javascript
form.reportValidity();
```

### 11.3 `setCustomValidity()`

Allows JavaScript to set a custom validation error message.

```html
<input type="text" id="username" required>

<script>
    const username = document.getElementById("username");

    username.addEventListener("input", function () {

        if (username.value.trim().length < 3) {
            username.setCustomValidity(
                "Username must contain at least 3 characters."
            );
        }
        else {
            username.setCustomValidity("");
        }

    });
</script>
```

**Important:** An empty string passed to `setCustomValidity("")` clears the custom validation error. If you do not clear it after the user corrects the input, the control remains invalid.

### 11.4 The `validity` property

The `validity` property exposes detailed information about a control's validation state.

Some useful properties:

| Property | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `valid` | Whether all constraints are satisfied |
| `valueMissing` | Required value is missing |
| `typeMismatch` | Value does not match the expected type |
| `tooShort` | Value is shorter than `minlength` |
| `tooLong` | Value exceeds `maxlength` |
| `rangeUnderflow` | Value is below `min` |
| `rangeOverflow` | Value is above `max` |
| `patternMismatch` | Value does not match `pattern` |
| `customError` | A custom validation error is set |

Example:

```javascript
const email = document.getElementById("email");

if (email.validity.typeMismatch) {
    console.log("Invalid email format");
}
```

