## 12. Important Form Concepts: `disabled` vs `readonly`

These attributes may look similar, but they behave differently.

| `disabled` | `readonly` |
|---|---|
| User cannot interact with the control | User cannot edit the value |
| Usually cannot receive focus | Can generally receive focus |
| Not included in form submission | Included in form submission when otherwise successful |
| Disabled controls are barred from constraint validation | Readonly controls are barred from constraint validation |

Example:

```html
<input type="text" name="username" value="Prajwal" readonly>

<input type="text" name="userId" value="101" disabled>
```

When the form is submitted, the readonly username can be included, but the disabled user ID is not included.

